  "id": "mastery-learning",
  "term": "mastery learning",
  "definition": "Mastery learning is an instructional approach in which progress is organized around achieving solid command of material before moving on. In the source, it is presented as part of a cognitively grounded teaching model intended to promote durable learning, alongside retrieval practice, adaptive sequencing, feedback, and instructional supports.",
